# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#  DesWatch — .gitignore
#  Covers: Node/TypeScript, VS Code extension
#  toolchain, VS Code editor, Claude Code,
#  Windows, and Ubuntu (Linux).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Node / npm ────────────────────────────────
# All third-party packages installed by npm.
# Never commit these; restore with `npm install`.
node_modules/

# npm debug logs written on failed installs.
npm-debug.log*

# Lockfile variants from other package managers.
# Commit package-lock.json; ignore yarn/pnpm locks
# so contributors aren't forced into a specific manager.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Optional npm cache directory if someone runs
# `npm install --cache .npm` inside the repo.
.npm/


# ── TypeScript build output ───────────────────
# The `out/` directory is produced by `tsc` as
# configured in tsconfig.json ("outDir": "out").
# It is regenerated on every compile run and must
# not be tracked — only source lives in the repo.
out/

# TypeScript incremental build cache.
# Speeds up subsequent compiles but is machine-specific.
*.tsbuildinfo


# ── VS Code extension packaging ───────────────
# .vsix files are the distributable bundles produced
# by `vsce package`. They are binary archives and
# should be attached to GitHub Releases, not committed.
*.vsix


# ── VS Code editor ────────────────────────────
# The .vscode/ folder holds workspace-level editor
# settings and launch configs.
#
# IMPORTANT: two files in this folder ARE intentionally
# committed for a consistent developer experience:
#   .vscode/launch.json   — F5 debug config for the extension host
#   .vscode/tasks.json    — build task wiring (npm run compile)
#
# Everything else (personal UI state, extension
# recommendations specific to one developer) is ignored.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# VS Code workspace file if one is ever created.
*.code-workspace


# ── Claude Code ───────────────────────────────
# Claude Code stores its project memory and session
# state in a hidden directory at the repo root.
# This is machine- and session-specific; never commit it.
.claude/

# HANDOFF.md at the repo root is the live working file
# produced by the current Claude Code session. It is
# ignored while in progress (transient, not yet reviewed).
#
# Convention: after each session, move and rename it into
# the handoffs/ directory before committing, e.g.:
#   handoffs/2026-05-19-phase-1.md
#
# The handoffs/ directory is NOT ignored — its contents
# form a permanent, human-readable project diary.
/HANDOFF.md


# ── Environment / secrets ─────────────────────
# .env files may contain API keys or publisher tokens.
# Never commit secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# ── Windows ───────────────────────────────────
# Thumbnail cache files created by Windows Explorer.
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db

# Windows shell metadata stored in every folder.
desktop.ini

# Shortcut files Windows sometimes drops into project dirs.
*.lnk

# Windows volume information (appears on root of drives).
$RECYCLE.BIN/


# ── Ubuntu / Linux ────────────────────────────
# macOS resource forks (in case a Mac joins the team).
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Vim swap / undo files (common on Linux dev machines).
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Linux trash folders.
.Trash-*/

# KDE / Dolphin folder metadata.
.directory


# ── Images ───────────────────────────────────
# The images/ directory holds the extension icon.
# Both the SVG source and the 128×128 PNG are committed:
#   images/icon.svg  — source, edit this
#   images/icon.png  — exported for the Marketplace (package.json "icon" field)
#
# Any other generated/resized variants are ignored.
images/*.png
!images/icon.png


# ── Miscellaneous ─────────────────────────────
# OS-agnostic editor backup files.
*.bak
*.orig

# Temporary files written by Claude Code's Edit tool on Windows.
*.ts.tmp.*